-- title:
--   The q+1 ends of the blow-up at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ and $\ell$ are primes with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\mid M'$ (hypotheses `hqM'`, `hℓ12`, `hℓM'`).
--
--   **Base field and level.** $L$ is a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L\subset L((t))$ is, by `hK`, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   **Coefficient ring and chart.** $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, an $L$-algebra which is a fraction ring of $A$, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero and has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the classical modular invariant (`hj`). Further, $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`). Here `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, `jChartFin` is $j$ viewed in it, `XFin A K j` is its spectrum, and `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` is the scheme obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and the $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras along the middle algebra, with `toBase` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and `ιFin` the canonical morphism from `XFin`.
--
--   **A supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The local rigidity hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of the two-chart model, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` above $z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, there exist: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, subject to six clauses: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every $\tau:K\simeq_L K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves the chart algebra; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$, the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart and trivial modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, $c\in W$ and $M\in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining the two chart-to-$S$ maps given by $\tau$, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\pmod\ell$, and $c\not\equiv1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) a branch-separation clause: two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions along $e$ composed with the completion map, provided $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) for such a prime $P$ with branch $(a,b)=(1,0)$ and every $a$ in the chart algebra, the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; and a final existential clause producing $j$-expansion data: `jqNModC L q` lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, an $a_0\in A$ with the difference in $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ part $\sum_{i\le e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and with $e$ of the germ of that difference equal to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The chosen point and its chart presentation.** Data $z,\varpi_z$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), $y'$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y : y'.asIdeal = y` fix a point as above. Then a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1\pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk at $z$ with $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$ are given, and `hW₁` asserts for this datum exactly the conjunction of the six clauses listed in `hArig`.
--
--   **The blow-up ideal and the blow-up algebra.** By `hJ`, the ideal $J$ of the chart algebra is the infimum of the ideals $J'$ obtained as follows: for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra, $J'$ is the pull-back along the restriction of $\tau$ of the contraction, along the composite of the germ map at $z$, the completion map and $e_1$, of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. By `hB`, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over the chart algebra by the set of $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$.
--
--   **The valuation ring and its properties.** $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). `hR1` states that the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$. `hR2` states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; that an element of the chart algebra lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; and that $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states: for any $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$, there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to\operatorname{ResidueField}A$, and equivariant for every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, via an element $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma,c)$ in the kernel `hSubgroup q` of $(g,c)\mapsto\det(g)c^{q+1}$ acting through `hAction`, with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit by the $\mathfrak m_W$-locus under some $\tau$ attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism preserving $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$.
--
--   **The distinguished automorphism.** Finally $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau_0$, a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$, satisfy $f\in W\iff\tau_0 f\in W$ for all $f\in K$ (`hτ₀W`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$ such that:
--
--   1. A subring $O\subseteq K$ belongs to `ends` if and only if there are $a$ in the chart algebra with $a\in J$ and $a\neq0$ in $K$, and, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over the chart algebra by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ xa=i\}$, a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ such that: $f\in O$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$; no element of $y$ which lies in $O$ is a unit of $O$; and $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   2. The cardinality of `ends` is $q+1$.
--
--   3. For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ satisfying $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$, and every $O\in$ `ends`, there is $O'\in$ `ends` with $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   4. For all $O,O'\in$ `ends` there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$ and $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   5. Every $O\in$ `ends` is preserved by $\tau_0$: $f\in O\iff\tau_0f\in O$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   6. For distinct $O,O'\in$ `ends` there is $f\in K$ lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$.
--
--   This is the step which identifies, at a supersingular closed point of the two-chart integral model of the modular function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, the $q+1$ branches ("ends") through that point after blowing up the ideal $J$: they are exactly the localisations of the blow-up charts described above, they number $q+1$, they are permuted transitively by the level automorphisms preserving the valuation ring $W$, each is fixed by the distinguished automorphism $\tau_0$, and distinct ends are separated by a function. It feeds the assembly result [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_cyclicDecomposition_ends_moduliHasse_igusaSepTranslate_commonChart_cover_blowupChart_linked_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_cyclicDecomposition_ends_moduliHasse_igusaSepTranslate_commonChart_cover_blowupChart_linked_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd), where the ends are organised into a cyclic decomposition covering the special fibre.
